From 4947ce61384cd37b699b889cfce81016e4d38cf4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sir-MmD <27060102+Sir-MmD@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:58:39 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] FireSafari: present as Safari on iPhone

- iPhone Safari user agent, platform and appVersion as GeckoView default prefs, so
  tabs, custom tabs, installed web apps, workers and service workers all report it.
  They are defaults: about:config (now enabled in all builds) can change them.
- Built-in ios-profile extension for page-visible Safari properties.
- Request desktop site sends Safari on Mac's user agent, as an iPhone does.
- Web-compat interventions keep their fixes but leave a Safari user agent alone.
